#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# hypergeometric_1f1

#% text
# `hypergeometric_1f1(a, b, z)` gives Kummer's confluent hypergeometric function `1F1(a; b; z)`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The series is the sum of `(a)_k/(b)_k*z^k/k!` (DLMF 13.2.2), an entire function of `z`.

#% item
# A non-positive integer `a` makes the series terminate; `1F1(a; a; z)` is `exp(z)`.

#% item
# Machine numbers, balls and complex numbers give numerical values. `hypergeometric_1f1` is listable.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
hypergeometric_1f1(1, 2, 1.0)
#% output
#= 1.7182818284590453

#% cell
hypergeometric_1f1(0.5, 1.5, -2.0)
#% output
#= 0.5981440066613041

#% cell
hypergeometric_1f1(-3, 1, 2.0)
#% output
#= -0.3333333333333333

#% cell
n(hypergeometric_1f1(1/2, 3/2, 1), 30)
#% output
#= 1.4626517459071816088040485868569882

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Large arguments:

#% cell
hypergeometric_1f1(1.0, 3.0, 50.0)
#% output
#= 4.147764422869658e18

#% text
# A complex argument:

#% cell
hypergeometric_1f1(1.0, 2.0, 1.0*im)
#% output
#= 0.8414709848078965 + 0.4596976941318603im

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# `1F1(1/2; 3/2; -x^2)` is `erf` up to a factor:

#% cell
hypergeometric_1f1(0.5, 1.5, -1.0) - sqrt(pi)/2*erf(1.0)
#% output
#= 0.0

#% text
# Kummer's transformation:

#% cell
hypergeometric_1f1(0.3, 1.7, 2.0) - exp(2.0)*hypergeometric_1f1(1.4, 1.7, -2.0)
#% output
#= -2.220446049250313e-16

#% subsection
# Possible issues

#% text
# Symbolic arguments stay unevaluated:

#% cell
hypergeometric_1f1(-3, 1, z)
#% output
#= 1 - 3*z + (3/2)*z^2 - (1/6)*z^3

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `hypergeometric_u`, `hypergeometric_2f1`, `hypergeometric_0f1`, `whittaker_m`
